# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
# Any .env variant, not just the exact name. Measured: a stale `.env.env.bak` holding real API
# keys sat beside `.env` and was matched by no ignore rule, so it was one `git add -A` away from
# being committed.
.env.*
*.env.bak
!.env.example

# --- Myriaxon state ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# This directory holds config.json with a live API key, the MCP server tokens, the messaging
# credentials, an audit log and a SQLite memory database. It must never be committed. The
# pre-rebrand name is listed too: an unmigrated tree still has it, and leaving it unmatched is
# how a credential ends up staged by an innocent `git add -A`.
.myriaxon/
.iohcode/

# --- Artifacts --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IQB-14 benchmark output (results carry traces and workspaces; not source)
bench-out/
# Scratch space for the harness's own unit tests
.bench-tmp/
# Ad-hoc eval logs
_probe_*.log
unit*.log
*.log

# --- A Locus's own output ------------------------------------------------------------------
# A locus created while the dashboard is open on this repository has THIS repository as its
# workspace, so when it is asked to write a document it writes it here. That is not a bug -- it is
# the workspace it was given -- but the result is generated prose sitting in a source tree, one
# `git add -A` away from being committed. Caught twice before this rule existed.
#
# The files are NOT deleted by this. They stay on disk; they are simply not source.
ANKER_*.md
*_VISION.md
*-proof.txt

# --- Editors / OS -----------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Terminal-Bench harness (tools/tb_*.py, tools/harbor_*.py) ------------------------------
# Large and regenerable, so none of it belongs in the repository:
#   .uv/            uv's cache, a downloaded CPython, the TB task set and the built wheel
#   .venv-harbor/   the Harbor framework's own virtualenv (needs Python 3.12; the agent needs 3.11)
#   jobs/           Harbor's per-trial artifacts -- logs and workspaces from benchmark runs
.uv/
.venv-harbor/
jobs/
pip-ephem-wheel-cache-*/
pip-modern-metadata-*/
# --- Extracted reference trees, archives, and scratch -------------------------------------
# The recovered .gitignore predated the comparison work, so none of this was covered: the four
# rival trees, the archives they came from, and the scratch directories a tool left behind.
# Measured at the time of the recovery: `git add -A` would have committed an extracted
# opencode tree and four source zips.
#
# `*-src/` is the RULE, matching the reasoning already recorded for the truncated third-party
# trees: the next source drop cannot slip hundreds of megabytes into a commit by being
# forgotten. The named entries are the ones that exist today.
*-src/
opencode-dev-src/
pi-harness-main-src/
openclaw-src/
claude-code-main-src/
deepseek-harness-master-src/
*.zip
tmp*/
pip-build-tracker-*/
pip-unpack-*/
pip-wheel-*/
myriaxon-tests-*/

# Scratch used while rebuilding after the wipe; not part of the tree.
.recovery/
.vendor/

# Local launcher variants for this machine only.
*-local.cmd
*-local.ps1

# Scratch files left by the documented examples in docs/HOW-TO-USE.md, so a reader
# following them does not accidentally commit one.
*-proof.txt
